UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>CompTIA CySA+ is a vendor-neutral, ANAB-accredited certification recognised by employers worldwide. This guide explains why that recognition is worth something, walks through every <strong>CS0-003</strong> exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,500 fee down substantially for eligible learners. Tertiary Infotech Academy is an <strong>Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner</strong> and a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, so you can train and sit the exam with us at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why a CompTIA certification carries weight</h2><p>There is no shortage of IT certificates. What separates CompTIA from a course-completion certificate is that the credential is <em>independently accredited and independently proctored</em> - and hiring managers know it.</p><ul><li><strong>Vendor-neutral by design.</strong> CompTIA certifies the principle, not one manufacturer''s console. A CompTIA CySA+ holder is expected to apply the concept in whatever stack the employer runs, which is why the credential survives a technology refresh.</li><li><strong>ISO 17024 accredited by ANAB.</strong> CompTIA''s core certifications are accredited to the international standard for personnel certification bodies. The exam is built to a documented job-task analysis, not to a syllabus someone invented.</li><li><strong>Recognised in government frameworks.</strong> Several CompTIA certifications are approved under the US Department of Defense 8140/8570 directive, a baseline that multinationals and defence-adjacent employers in Singapore routinely mirror in their own hiring standards.</li><li><strong>Performance-based questions.</strong> CompTIA exams do not only ask you to recognise the right answer. Performance-based items drop you into a simulated environment and require you to complete the task, which is far harder to pass on memorisation alone.</li><li><strong>Portable across borders.</strong> The certification means the same thing in Singapore, Sydney or London - useful in a market where regional mobility is common.</li></ul><p>CySA+ is the analyst credential that sits between Security+ and SecurityX. Where Security+ proves you know the controls, CySA+ proves you can read the telemetry - triaging alerts, hunting threats and running an incident to closure. It is the credential SOC hiring managers ask for.</p><h2>The CS0-003 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>CompTIA CySA+</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>CS0-003</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Intermediate / blue team analyst</td></tr><tr><th>Questions</th><td>Maximum 85 questions (multiple choice and performance-based)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>165 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>750 on a scale of 100-900</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> CompTIA recommends Security+ or Network+ plus around four years of hands-on security or incident response experience, though neither is enforced.</p><h2>CS0-003 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>The weightings tell you where to spend your study time. Read them as a revision budget: the heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Security Operations</strong></td><td>33%</td><td>The largest domain: system and network architecture concepts, analysing indicators of malicious activity across host, network, application and cloud, threat intelligence and threat hunting, and the tooling and automation that support efficient security operations.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vulnerability Management</strong></td><td>30%</td><td>Implementing vulnerability scanning, analysing output and validating findings, prioritising with CVSS and contextual risk factors, and recommending controls to mitigate what the scan found.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Incident Response and Management</strong></td><td>20%</td><td>Attack frameworks such as MITRE ATT&amp;CK and the Cyber Kill Chain, the incident response lifecycle, containment, eradication and recovery, and post-incident activities.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reporting and Communication</strong></td><td>17%</td><td>Vulnerability management reporting, stakeholder communication, compliance reporting, action plans, and articulating risk to a non-technical audience.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-cybersecurity-analyst-cysa-training.html">WSQ - CompTIA Cybersecurity Analyst (CySA+) Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the CS0-003 objectives above. It is delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme, it carries the funding described below and is assessed - you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> SOC Analyst (Tier 1-2), Threat Intelligence Analyst, Incident Response Analyst, Vulnerability Analyst, Security Operations Engineer.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>CS0-003</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse CS0-003 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>How much will you actually pay? Funding for CompTIA CySA+ training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024049211</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,500</strong> is not what most learners pay. Several schemes stack, and they are applied in a specific order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against whatever is left.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Subsidy is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the one restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024049211" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024049211.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024049211" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff for this course may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>All funding is subject to eligibility and to the prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement. Talk to us before you enrol and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Confirm your citizenship, age band and whether your employer is sponsoring you - this determines whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-cybersecurity-analyst-cysa-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Attend the instructor-led training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Buy your exam voucher.</strong> Purchase the CS0-003 voucher through us.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam at our Pearson VUE test centre.</strong> Book a proctored slot at our centre while the material is fresh.</li><li><strong>Submit your claims.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers the instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The CS0-003 exam voucher is purchased separately - we supply CompTIA vouchers at among the lowest prices in Singapore, and you can sit the exam at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need to pass the exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding is tied to attending the course and passing the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not the CompTIA exam. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and being assessed competent secures the subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What do I actually pay after funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>It depends on your profile. Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to what remains. Contact us with your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the CompTIA exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network. You can register and sit your proctored CS0-003 exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the prerequisites before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>CompTIA recommends Security+ or Network+ plus around four years of hands-on security or incident response experience, though neither is enforced. CompTIA recommendations are guidance rather than gates - nothing blocks you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a level lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for CompTIA CySA+ training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View the upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-cybersecurity-analyst-cysa-training.html"><strong>WSQ - CompTIA Cybersecurity Analyst (CySA+) Training</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-comptia-cysa-plus-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>CompTIA A+ is a vendor-neutral, ANAB-accredited certification recognised by employers worldwide. This guide explains why that recognition is worth something, walks through every <strong>220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2)</strong> exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,000 fee down substantially for eligible learners. Tertiary Infotech Academy is an <strong>Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner</strong> and a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, so you can train and sit the exam with us at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why a CompTIA certification carries weight</h2><p>There is no shortage of IT certificates. What separates CompTIA from a course-completion certificate is that the credential is <em>independently accredited and independently proctored</em> - and hiring managers know it.</p><ul><li><strong>Vendor-neutral by design.</strong> CompTIA certifies the principle, not one manufacturer''s console. A CompTIA A+ holder is expected to apply the concept in whatever stack the employer runs, which is why the credential survives a technology refresh.</li><li><strong>ISO 17024 accredited by ANAB.</strong> CompTIA''s core certifications are accredited to the international standard for personnel certification bodies. The exam is built to a documented job-task analysis, not to a syllabus someone invented.</li><li><strong>Recognised in government frameworks.</strong> Several CompTIA certifications are approved under the US Department of Defense 8140/8570 directive, a baseline that multinationals and defence-adjacent employers in Singapore routinely mirror in their own hiring standards.</li><li><strong>Performance-based questions.</strong> CompTIA exams do not only ask you to recognise the right answer. Performance-based items drop you into a simulated environment and require you to complete the task, which is far harder to pass on memorisation alone.</li><li><strong>Portable across borders.</strong> The certification means the same thing in Singapore, Sydney or London - useful in a market where regional mobility is common.</li></ul><p>A+ appears in more tech support job listings than any other IT credential and is the only entry-level certification with performance-based testing, so it proves you can actually perform the task rather than recognise the right answer. It is the standard first rung of an IT career.</p><h2>The 220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2) exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>CompTIA A+</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Entry / IT support foundation</td></tr><tr><th>Questions</th><td>Maximum 90 questions per exam (multiple choice and performance-based)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>90 minutes per exam</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>675 for Core 1 and 700 for Core 2, on a scale of 100-900</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> No formal prerequisites. CompTIA suggests around nine to twelve months of hands-on experience, but A+ is designed as the entry point.</p><h2>220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2) exam domains and weightings</h2><p>The weightings tell you where to spend your study time. Read them as a revision budget: the heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Core 1: Mobile Devices</strong></td><td>15%</td><td>Installing and configuring laptop hardware, mobile device components, accessories and network connectivity including cellular and synchronisation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Core 1: Networking</strong></td><td>20%</td><td>TCP/IP fundamentals, common ports and protocols, networking hardware, wireless standards, and configuring SOHO networks.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Core 1: Hardware</strong></td><td>25%</td><td>Cables and connectors, motherboards, CPUs, RAM, power supplies, storage, printers and multifunction devices.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Core 1: Virtualisation and Cloud Computing</strong></td><td>11%</td><td>Cloud service and deployment models, and client-side virtualisation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Core 1: Hardware and Network Troubleshooting</strong></td><td>29%</td><td>Applying a structured troubleshooting methodology to hardware, storage, display, networking and printer faults.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Core 2: Operating Systems</strong></td><td>31%</td><td>Windows, macOS, Linux, Android and iOS - installation, configuration, command line tools and OS features.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Core 2: Security</strong></td><td>25%</td><td>Physical and logical security measures, wireless security, malware detection and removal, social engineering, and workstation and mobile device hardening.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Core 2: Software Troubleshooting</strong></td><td>22%</td><td>Resolving Windows OS problems, application issues, mobile OS faults and malware symptoms.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Core 2: Operational Procedures</strong></td><td>22%</td><td>Documentation and change management, backup and recovery, safety and environmental controls, incident response, communication and professionalism, and basic scripting.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Note that A+ requires you to pass <strong>both</strong> Core 1 (220-1101) and Core 2 (220-1102). They are sat as two separate exams and you are only certified once both are complete. There is no requirement to sit them on the same day.</p><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-a-training-core-1-and-core-2.html">WSQ - CompTIA Certified A+ Training (Core 1 and Core 2)</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the 220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2) objectives above. It is delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme, it carries the funding described below and is assessed - you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> IT Support Specialist, Help Desk Technician, Desktop Support Analyst, Field Service Technician, Associate Network Engineer.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2)</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse 220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2) questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>How much will you actually pay? Funding for CompTIA A+ training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024048317</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. Several schemes stack, and they are applied in a specific order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against whatever is left.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Subsidy is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the one restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024048317" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024048317.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024048317" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff for this course may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>All funding is subject to eligibility and to the prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement. Talk to us before you enrol and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Confirm your citizenship, age band and whether your employer is sponsoring you - this determines whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-a-training-core-1-and-core-2.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Attend the instructor-led training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Buy your exam voucher.</strong> Purchase the 220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2) voucher through us.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam at our Pearson VUE test centre.</strong> Book a proctored slot at our centre while the material is fresh.</li><li><strong>Submit your claims.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers the instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The 220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2) exam voucher is purchased separately - we supply CompTIA vouchers at among the lowest prices in Singapore, and you can sit the exam at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need to pass the exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding is tied to attending the course and passing the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not the CompTIA exam. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and being assessed competent secures the subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What do I actually pay after funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>It depends on your profile. Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit and PSEA can be applied to what remains. Contact us with your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the CompTIA exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network. You can register and sit your proctored 220-1101 (Core 1) and 220-1102 (Core 2) exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the prerequisites before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No formal prerequisites. CompTIA suggests around nine to twelve months of hands-on experience, but A+ is designed as the entry point. CompTIA recommendations are guidance rather than gates - nothing blocks you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a level lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for CompTIA A+ training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View the upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-a-training-core-1-and-core-2.html"><strong>WSQ - CompTIA Certified A+ Training (Core 1 and Core 2)</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-comptia-a-plus-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>CompTIA Cloud+ is a vendor-neutral, ANAB-accredited certification recognised by employers worldwide. This guide explains why that recognition is worth something, walks through every <strong>CV0-004</strong> exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,000 fee down substantially for eligible learners. Tertiary Infotech Academy is an <strong>Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner</strong> and a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, so you can train and sit the exam with us at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why a CompTIA certification carries weight</h2><p>There is no shortage of IT certificates. What separates CompTIA from a course-completion certificate is that the credential is <em>independently accredited and independently proctored</em> - and hiring managers know it.</p><ul><li><strong>Vendor-neutral by design.</strong> CompTIA certifies the principle, not one manufacturer''s console. A CompTIA Cloud+ holder is expected to apply the concept in whatever stack the employer runs, which is why the credential survives a technology refresh.</li><li><strong>ISO 17024 accredited by ANAB.</strong> CompTIA''s core certifications are accredited to the international standard for personnel certification bodies. The exam is built to a documented job-task analysis, not to a syllabus someone invented.</li><li><strong>Recognised in government frameworks.</strong> Several CompTIA certifications are approved under the US Department of Defense 8140/8570 directive, a baseline that multinationals and defence-adjacent employers in Singapore routinely mirror in their own hiring standards.</li><li><strong>Performance-based questions.</strong> CompTIA exams do not only ask you to recognise the right answer. Performance-based items drop you into a simulated environment and require you to complete the task, which is far harder to pass on memorisation alone.</li><li><strong>Portable across borders.</strong> The certification means the same thing in Singapore, Sydney or London - useful in a market where regional mobility is common.</li></ul><p>Cloud+ is the only major cloud certification that is genuinely vendor-neutral - it validates cloud operations across AWS, Azure and Google Cloud rather than one provider''s console. That matters in Singapore, where most enterprises now run multi-cloud or hybrid estates.</p><h2>The CV0-004 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>CompTIA Cloud+</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>CV0-004</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Intermediate / cloud operations</td></tr><tr><th>Questions</th><td>Maximum 90 questions (multiple choice and performance-based)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>90 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>Pass/fail only - no scaled score is reported</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> CompTIA recommends Network+ or Server+ plus around two to three years of systems, networking or cloud administration experience, though neither is enforced.</p><h2>CV0-004 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>The weightings tell you where to spend your study time. Read them as a revision budget: the heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Cloud Architecture</strong></td><td>23%</td><td>Cloud deployment and service models, shared responsibility, capacity planning, high availability and scaling, and designing solutions that meet stated business requirements.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Deployment</strong></td><td>20%</td><td>Provisioning compute, storage and networking; integrating infrastructure as code and CI/CD; migrating workloads; and configuring cloud-native and containerised environments.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Operations</strong></td><td>22%</td><td>Monitoring, logging and alerting; performance and cost optimisation (FinOps); backup, disaster recovery and business continuity; and lifecycle and change management.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security</strong></td><td>18%</td><td>Identity and access management, network and data security, encryption and key management, compliance frameworks and cloud security posture.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>DevOps Fundamentals</strong></td><td>17%</td><td>Automation and orchestration, configuration management, containers and orchestration platforms, and the API-driven tooling that underpins modern cloud delivery.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-cloud-training.html">WSQ - CompTIA Certified Cloud+ Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the CV0-004 objectives above. It is delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme, it carries the funding described below and is assessed - you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Cloud Engineer, Cloud Administrator, Systems Engineer, DevOps Engineer, Cloud Operations Analyst.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>CV0-004</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse CV0-004 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>How much will you actually pay? Funding for CompTIA Cloud+ training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024049214</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. Several schemes stack, and they are applied in a specific order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against whatever is left.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Subsidy is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the one restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024049214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024049214.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024049214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff for this course may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>All funding is subject to eligibility and to the prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement. Talk to us before you enrol and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Confirm your citizenship, age band and whether your employer is sponsoring you - this determines whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-cloud-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Attend the instructor-led training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Buy your exam voucher.</strong> Purchase the CV0-004 voucher through us.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam at our Pearson VUE test centre.</strong> Book a proctored slot at our centre while the material is fresh.</li><li><strong>Submit your claims.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers the instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The CV0-004 exam voucher is purchased separately - we supply CompTIA vouchers at among the lowest prices in Singapore, and you can sit the exam at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need to pass the exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding is tied to attending the course and passing the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not the CompTIA exam. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and being assessed competent secures the subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What do I actually pay after funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>It depends on your profile. Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to what remains. Contact us with your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the CompTIA exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network. You can register and sit your proctored CV0-004 exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the prerequisites before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>CompTIA recommends Network+ or Server+ plus around two to three years of systems, networking or cloud administration experience, though neither is enforced. CompTIA recommendations are guidance rather than gates - nothing blocks you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a level lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for CompTIA Cloud+ training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View the upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-cloud-training.html"><strong>WSQ - CompTIA Certified Cloud+ Training</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-comptia-cloud-plus-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>CompTIA Data+ is a vendor-neutral, ANAB-accredited certification recognised by employers worldwide. This guide explains why that recognition is worth something, walks through every <strong>DA0-001</strong> exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,000 fee down substantially for eligible learners. Tertiary Infotech Academy is an <strong>Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner</strong> and a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, so you can train and sit the exam with us at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why a CompTIA certification carries weight</h2><p>There is no shortage of IT certificates. What separates CompTIA from a course-completion certificate is that the credential is <em>independently accredited and independently proctored</em> - and hiring managers know it.</p><ul><li><strong>Vendor-neutral by design.</strong> CompTIA certifies the principle, not one manufacturer''s console. A CompTIA Data+ holder is expected to apply the concept in whatever stack the employer runs, which is why the credential survives a technology refresh.</li><li><strong>ISO 17024 accredited by ANAB.</strong> CompTIA''s core certifications are accredited to the international standard for personnel certification bodies. The exam is built to a documented job-task analysis, not to a syllabus someone invented.</li><li><strong>Recognised in government frameworks.</strong> Several CompTIA certifications are approved under the US Department of Defense 8140/8570 directive, a baseline that multinationals and defence-adjacent employers in Singapore routinely mirror in their own hiring standards.</li><li><strong>Performance-based questions.</strong> CompTIA exams do not only ask you to recognise the right answer. Performance-based items drop you into a simulated environment and require you to complete the task, which is far harder to pass on memorisation alone.</li><li><strong>Portable across borders.</strong> The certification means the same thing in Singapore, Sydney or London - useful in a market where regional mobility is common.</li></ul><p>Data+ is vendor-neutral and analyst-focused: it certifies the full workflow from mining and cleaning through analysis to the dashboard, rather than proficiency in one BI tool. For professionals moving into analytics from a business function, it is a credible signal that does not require a computer science background.</p><h2>The DA0-001 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>CompTIA Data+</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>DA0-001</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Early-career data analyst</td></tr><tr><th>Questions</th><td>Maximum 90 questions (multiple choice and performance-based)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>90 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>675 on a scale of 100-900</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> CompTIA recommends around eighteen to twenty-four months of experience in a report or business analyst role, plus exposure to databases and analytics tools. Not enforced.</p><h2>DA0-001 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>The weightings tell you where to spend your study time. Read them as a revision budget: the heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Data Concepts and Environments</strong></td><td>15%</td><td>Identifying basic data types and structures, and understanding the database systems, data warehouses and processing environments analysts work in.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Data Mining</strong></td><td>25%</td><td>Data acquisition, integration and cleansing; profiling and manipulating datasets; and applying the query and preparation techniques that consume most of an analyst''s day.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Data Analysis</strong></td><td>23%</td><td>Applying descriptive statistics, hypothesis testing and analytics techniques to identify trends, correlations and patterns that answer a business question.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Visualisation</strong></td><td>23%</td><td>Designing reports and dashboards, selecting the right chart for the message, and translating analytical output into a form a stakeholder can act on.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Data Governance, Quality and Controls</strong></td><td>14%</td><td>Data governance concepts, quality control measures, master data management, and the privacy and regulatory obligations that constrain analytics work.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-data-training.html">WSQ - CompTIA Certified Data+ Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the DA0-001 objectives above. It is delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme, it carries the funding described below and is assessed - you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Data Analyst, Business Analyst, Reporting Analyst, Business Intelligence Analyst, Operations Analyst, Marketing Analyst.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>DA0-001</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse DA0-001 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>How much will you actually pay? Funding for CompTIA Data+ training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024049212</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. Several schemes stack, and they are applied in a specific order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against whatever is left.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Subsidy is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the one restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024049212" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024049212.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024049212" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff for this course may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>All funding is subject to eligibility and to the prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement. Talk to us before you enrol and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Confirm your citizenship, age band and whether your employer is sponsoring you - this determines whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-data-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Attend the instructor-led training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Buy your exam voucher.</strong> Purchase the DA0-001 voucher through us.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam at our Pearson VUE test centre.</strong> Book a proctored slot at our centre while the material is fresh.</li><li><strong>Submit your claims.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers the instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The DA0-001 exam voucher is purchased separately - we supply CompTIA vouchers at among the lowest prices in Singapore, and you can sit the exam at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need to pass the exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding is tied to attending the course and passing the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not the CompTIA exam. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and being assessed competent secures the subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What do I actually pay after funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>It depends on your profile. Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to what remains. Contact us with your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the CompTIA exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network. You can register and sit your proctored DA0-001 exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the prerequisites before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>CompTIA recommends around eighteen to twenty-four months of experience in a report or business analyst role, plus exposure to databases and analytics tools. Not enforced. CompTIA recommendations are guidance rather than gates - nothing blocks you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a level lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for CompTIA Data+ training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View the upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-data-training.html"><strong>WSQ - CompTIA Certified Data+ Training</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>'
