UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>CompTIA Linux+ is a vendor-neutral, ANAB-accredited certification recognised by employers worldwide. This guide explains why that recognition is worth something, walks through every <strong>XK0-005</strong> exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,000 fee down substantially for eligible learners. Tertiary Infotech Academy is an <strong>Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner</strong> and a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, so you can train and sit the exam with us at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why a CompTIA certification carries weight</h2><p>There is no shortage of IT certificates. What separates CompTIA from a course-completion certificate is that the credential is <em>independently accredited and independently proctored</em> - and hiring managers know it.</p><ul><li><strong>Vendor-neutral by design.</strong> CompTIA certifies the principle, not one manufacturer''s console. A CompTIA Linux+ holder is expected to apply the concept in whatever stack the employer runs, which is why the credential survives a technology refresh.</li><li><strong>ISO 17024 accredited by ANAB.</strong> CompTIA''s core certifications are accredited to the international standard for personnel certification bodies. The exam is built to a documented job-task analysis, not to a syllabus someone invented.</li><li><strong>Recognised in government frameworks.</strong> Several CompTIA certifications are approved under the US Department of Defense 8140/8570 directive, a baseline that multinationals and defence-adjacent employers in Singapore routinely mirror in their own hiring standards.</li><li><strong>Performance-based questions.</strong> CompTIA exams do not only ask you to recognise the right answer. Performance-based items drop you into a simulated environment and require you to complete the task, which is far harder to pass on memorisation alone.</li><li><strong>Portable across borders.</strong> The certification means the same thing in Singapore, Sydney or London - useful in a market where regional mobility is common.</li></ul><p>Linux runs the overwhelming majority of cloud workloads, containers and web infrastructure, and Linux+ is the vendor-neutral proof that you can administer it across distributions rather than only on Red Hat or only on Ubuntu. Its coverage of scripting, containers and automation makes it a genuine DevOps on-ramp.</p><h2>The XK0-005 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>CompTIA Linux+</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>XK0-005</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Intermediate / Linux system administration</td></tr><tr><th>Questions</th><td>Maximum 90 questions (multiple choice and performance-based)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>90 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>720 on a scale of 100-900</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> CompTIA recommends A+, Network+ and Server+ plus around twelve months of hands-on Linux administration experience. Not enforced.</p><h2>XK0-005 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>The weightings tell you where to spend your study time. Read them as a revision budget: the heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>System Management</strong></td><td>32%</td><td>The largest domain: managing software and services, storage and filesystems, users and groups, permissions and ownership, kernel modules, network configuration and the Linux boot process.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security</strong></td><td>21%</td><td>Applying and configuring permissions, access controls including SELinux and AppArmor, firewalls, SSH and certificate management, and logging and auditing.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Scripting, Containers and Automation</strong></td><td>19%</td><td>Bash scripting constructs, version control with Git, container management, and infrastructure automation and orchestration tooling.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Troubleshooting</strong></td><td>28%</td><td>Diagnosing storage, network, CPU and memory, user access, filesystem and service faults using systemd, journald and the standard command line toolkit.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-linux-training.html">WSQ - CompTIA Certified Linux+ Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the XK0-005 objectives above. It is delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme, it carries the funding described below and is assessed - you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Linux Administrator, Systems Administrator, DevOps Engineer, Site Reliability Engineer, Cloud Engineer, Network Administrator.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>XK0-005</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse XK0-005 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>How much will you actually pay? Funding for CompTIA Linux+ training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024048316</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. Several schemes stack, and they are applied in a specific order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against whatever is left.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Subsidy is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the one restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024048316" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024048316.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024048316" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff for this course may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>All funding is subject to eligibility and to the prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement. Talk to us before you enrol and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Confirm your citizenship, age band and whether your employer is sponsoring you - this determines whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-linux-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Attend the instructor-led training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Buy your exam voucher.</strong> Purchase the XK0-005 voucher through us.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam at our Pearson VUE test centre.</strong> Book a proctored slot at our centre while the material is fresh.</li><li><strong>Submit your claims.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers the instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The XK0-005 exam voucher is purchased separately - we supply CompTIA vouchers at among the lowest prices in Singapore, and you can sit the exam at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need to pass the exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding is tied to attending the course and passing the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not the CompTIA exam. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and being assessed competent secures the subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What do I actually pay after funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>It depends on your profile. Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to what remains. Contact us with your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the CompTIA exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network. You can register and sit your proctored XK0-005 exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the prerequisites before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>CompTIA recommends A+, Network+ and Server+ plus around twelve months of hands-on Linux administration experience. Not enforced. CompTIA recommendations are guidance rather than gates - nothing blocks you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a level lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for CompTIA Linux+ training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View the upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-linux-training.html"><strong>WSQ - CompTIA Certified Linux+ Training</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-comptia-linux-plus-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>CompTIA Server+ is a vendor-neutral, ANAB-accredited certification recognised by employers worldwide. This guide explains why that recognition is worth something, walks through every <strong>SK0-005</strong> exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,000 fee down substantially for eligible learners. Tertiary Infotech Academy is an <strong>Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner</strong> and a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, so you can train and sit the exam with us at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why a CompTIA certification carries weight</h2><p>There is no shortage of IT certificates. What separates CompTIA from a course-completion certificate is that the credential is <em>independently accredited and independently proctored</em> - and hiring managers know it.</p><ul><li><strong>Vendor-neutral by design.</strong> CompTIA certifies the principle, not one manufacturer''s console. A CompTIA Server+ holder is expected to apply the concept in whatever stack the employer runs, which is why the credential survives a technology refresh.</li><li><strong>ISO 17024 accredited by ANAB.</strong> CompTIA''s core certifications are accredited to the international standard for personnel certification bodies. The exam is built to a documented job-task analysis, not to a syllabus someone invented.</li><li><strong>Recognised in government frameworks.</strong> Several CompTIA certifications are approved under the US Department of Defense 8140/8570 directive, a baseline that multinationals and defence-adjacent employers in Singapore routinely mirror in their own hiring standards.</li><li><strong>Performance-based questions.</strong> CompTIA exams do not only ask you to recognise the right answer. Performance-based items drop you into a simulated environment and require you to complete the task, which is far harder to pass on memorisation alone.</li><li><strong>Portable across borders.</strong> The certification means the same thing in Singapore, Sydney or London - useful in a market where regional mobility is common.</li></ul><p>Server+ is the only major server certification with no vendor lock-in and, uniquely in the CompTIA portfolio, it does not expire - the SK0-005 credential is issued for life. For data centre and infrastructure roles it covers the hardware, virtualisation, storage and disaster recovery ground that OS-specific certifications skip.</p><h2>The SK0-005 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>CompTIA Server+</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>SK0-005</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Intermediate / server administration</td></tr><tr><th>Questions</th><td>Maximum 90 questions (multiple choice and performance-based)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>90 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>750 on a scale of 100-900</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Does not expire - Server+ is a lifetime certification for exams taken from SK0-005 onwards</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> CompTIA recommends A+ plus around two years of hands-on server or data centre experience. Not enforced.</p><h2>SK0-005 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>The weightings tell you where to spend your study time. Read them as a revision budget: the heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Server Hardware Installation and Management</strong></td><td>18%</td><td>Server form factors and components, rack installation and power, storage technologies and RAID levels, and hardware maintenance and lifecycle.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Server Administration</strong></td><td>30%</td><td>The largest domain: installing and configuring server operating systems, virtualisation and cloud integration, licensing, asset management, documentation and change control.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security and Disaster Recovery</strong></td><td>24%</td><td>Physical and logical server security, data security and encryption, hardening, backup methodologies, replication and disaster recovery planning.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Troubleshooting</strong></td><td>28%</td><td>Applying a structured methodology to hardware, OS, storage, network and security faults, including boot and performance problems.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-server-training.html">WSQ - CompTIA Certified Server+ Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the SK0-005 objectives above. It is delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme, it carries the funding described below and is assessed - you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Server Administrator, Systems Administrator, Data Centre Technician, Infrastructure Engineer, Network Administrator.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>SK0-005</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse SK0-005 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>How much will you actually pay? Funding for CompTIA Server+ training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024048318</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. Several schemes stack, and they are applied in a specific order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against whatever is left.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Subsidy is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the one restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024048318" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024048318.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024048318" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff for this course may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>All funding is subject to eligibility and to the prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement. Talk to us before you enrol and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Confirm your citizenship, age band and whether your employer is sponsoring you - this determines whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-server-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Attend the instructor-led training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Buy your exam voucher.</strong> Purchase the SK0-005 voucher through us.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam at our Pearson VUE test centre.</strong> Book a proctored slot at our centre while the material is fresh.</li><li><strong>Submit your claims.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers the instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The SK0-005 exam voucher is purchased separately - we supply CompTIA vouchers at among the lowest prices in Singapore, and you can sit the exam at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need to pass the exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding is tied to attending the course and passing the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not the CompTIA exam. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and being assessed competent secures the subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What do I actually pay after funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>It depends on your profile. Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to what remains. Contact us with your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the CompTIA exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network. You can register and sit your proctored SK0-005 exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the prerequisites before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>CompTIA recommends A+ plus around two years of hands-on server or data centre experience. Not enforced. CompTIA recommendations are guidance rather than gates - nothing blocks you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a level lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Does not expire - Server+ is a lifetime certification for exams taken from SK0-005 onwards</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for CompTIA Server+ training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View the upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-comptia-certified-server-training.html"><strong>WSQ - CompTIA Certified Server+ Training</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-comptia-server-plus-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>CompTIA PenTest+ is a vendor-neutral, ANAB-accredited certification recognised by employers worldwide. This guide explains why that recognition is worth something, walks through every <strong>PT0-003</strong> exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$3,000 fee down substantially for eligible learners. Tertiary Infotech Academy is an <strong>Authorised CompTIA Delivery Partner</strong> and a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, so you can train and sit the exam with us at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why a CompTIA certification carries weight</h2><p>There is no shortage of IT certificates. What separates CompTIA from a course-completion certificate is that the credential is <em>independently accredited and independently proctored</em> - and hiring managers know it.</p><ul><li><strong>Vendor-neutral by design.</strong> CompTIA certifies the principle, not one manufacturer''s console. A CompTIA PenTest+ holder is expected to apply the concept in whatever stack the employer runs, which is why the credential survives a technology refresh.</li><li><strong>ISO 17024 accredited by ANAB.</strong> CompTIA''s core certifications are accredited to the international standard for personnel certification bodies. The exam is built to a documented job-task analysis, not to a syllabus someone invented.</li><li><strong>Recognised in government frameworks.</strong> Several CompTIA certifications are approved under the US Department of Defense 8140/8570 directive, a baseline that multinationals and defence-adjacent employers in Singapore routinely mirror in their own hiring standards.</li><li><strong>Performance-based questions.</strong> CompTIA exams do not only ask you to recognise the right answer. Performance-based items drop you into a simulated environment and require you to complete the task, which is far harder to pass on memorisation alone.</li><li><strong>Portable across borders.</strong> The certification means the same thing in Singapore, Sydney or London - useful in a market where regional mobility is common.</li></ul><p>PenTest+ is the only offensive security certification that assesses both the hands-on attack skills and the engagement management around them - scoping, legal agreements, reporting and remediation advice. That second half is what separates a professional pen tester from someone who can run an exploit.</p><h2>The PT0-003 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>CompTIA PenTest+</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>PT0-003</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Intermediate / offensive security</td></tr><tr><th>Questions</th><td>Maximum 90 questions (multiple choice and performance-based)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>165 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>750 on a scale of 100-900</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> CompTIA recommends Network+ and Security+ or equivalent, plus around three to four years of hands-on information security experience. Not enforced.</p><h2>PT0-003 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>The weightings tell you where to spend your study time. Read them as a revision budget: the heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Engagement Management</strong></td><td>13%</td><td>Pre-engagement activities, scoping and rules of engagement, legal and compliance considerations, collaboration and communication, and professional reporting of findings and recommendations.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reconnaissance and Enumeration</strong></td><td>21%</td><td>Passive and active reconnaissance, OSINT, scanning and enumeration with tools such as Nmap and Wireshark, and preparing a target profile from the data gathered.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vulnerability Discovery and Analysis</strong></td><td>17%</td><td>Conducting vulnerability scans, analysing and validating output to eliminate false positives, prioritising by exploitability and business impact, and physical and social engineering assessment.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Attacks and Exploits</strong></td><td>35%</td><td>The largest domain: exploiting network, wireless, application, cloud, host and authentication weaknesses; social engineering; and post-exploitation activities including persistence and lateral movement.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Post-exploitation and Lateral Movement</strong></td><td>14%</td><td>Establishing and maintaining footholds, escalating privileges, moving laterally, and - critically - cleaning up artefacts to leave the environment as it was found.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the CASL course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/casl-comptia-pentest-training.html">CASL - CompTIA PenTest+ Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the PT0-003 objectives above. It is delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a CASL-approved programme, it carries the funding described below and is assessed - you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Penetration Tester, Red Team Operator, Vulnerability Assessment Analyst, Security Consultant, Application Security Analyst.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>PT0-003</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse PT0-003 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>How much will you actually pay? Funding for CompTIA PenTest+ training</h2><p>This is a <strong>CASL-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2026064471</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$3,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. Several schemes stack, and they are applied in a specific order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against whatever is left.</p><h3>1. Baseline CASL course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Subsidy is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the one restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2026064471" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2026064471.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2026064471" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff for this course may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>All funding is subject to eligibility and to the prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement. Talk to us before you enrol and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Confirm your citizenship, age band and whether your employer is sponsoring you - this determines whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/casl-comptia-pentest-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Attend the instructor-led training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the CASL assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Buy your exam voucher.</strong> Purchase the PT0-003 voucher through us.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam at our Pearson VUE test centre.</strong> Book a proctored slot at our centre while the material is fresh.</li><li><strong>Submit your claims.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the exam included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers the instructor-led training, courseware and the CASL assessment. The PT0-003 exam voucher is purchased separately - we supply CompTIA vouchers at among the lowest prices in Singapore, and you can sit the exam at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need to pass the exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding is tied to attending the course and passing the <em>CASL assessment</em>, not the CompTIA exam. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and being assessed competent secures the subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What do I actually pay after funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>It depends on your profile. Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to what remains. Contact us with your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the CompTIA exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center, and CompTIA exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network. You can register and sit your proctored PT0-003 exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the prerequisites before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>CompTIA recommends Network+ and Security+ or equivalent, plus around three to four years of hands-on information security experience. Not enforced. CompTIA recommendations are guidance rather than gates - nothing blocks you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a level lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years, renewable through CompTIA''s Continuing Education programme</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for CompTIA PenTest+ training</h2><p>Seats are limited and classes fill ahead of each intake. View the upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/casl-comptia-pentest-training.html"><strong>CASL - CompTIA PenTest+ Training</strong></a> course page, or call us on +65 6100 0613 if you would like your funding worked out first.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'casl-comptia-pentest-plus-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner is an foundational-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>CLF-C02</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$800 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking CLF-C02.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 100</strong> and takes 90 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>Cloud Practitioner is the credential that proves cloud literacy without requiring you to be an engineer. It is the fastest way for a non-technical professional to become credible in cloud conversations, and the standard first step before any associate-level AWS certification.</p><h2>The CLF-C02 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>CLF-C02</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Foundational</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>65 questions (multiple choice and multiple response)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>90 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>700 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 100 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> No prerequisites. AWS suggests up to six months of general AWS exposure, but this is explicitly designed as the entry point for technical and non-technical learners alike.</p><h2>CLF-C02 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Cloud Concepts</strong></td><td>24%</td><td>The value proposition of the AWS Cloud, the design principles of the Well-Architected Framework, cloud migration strategies and the economics of cloud adoption.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security and Compliance</strong></td><td>30%</td><td>The largest domain: the AWS shared responsibility model, security and compliance governance, IAM access management, and the security components AWS provides.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cloud Technology and Services</strong></td><td>34%</td><td>Methods of deploying and operating in AWS, global infrastructure (Regions, Availability Zones, edge locations), and the core compute, storage, networking, database and AI service families.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Billing, Pricing and Support</strong></td><td>12%</td><td>AWS pricing models, cost management and budgeting tools, billing structures, and the AWS support plans and technical resources available.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-cloud-practitioner-training.html">WSQ - AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the CLF-C02 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Cloud Sales and Procurement, Project Manager, Business Analyst, IT Support, anyone in a cloud-adjacent role.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>CLF-C02</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse CLF-C02 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2023039183</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$800</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2023039183" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2023039183.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2023039183" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 100 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-cloud-practitioner-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule CLF-C02 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The CLF-C02 exam costs USD 100 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule CLF-C02 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No prerequisites. AWS suggests up to six months of general AWS exposure, but this is explicitly designed as the entry point for technical and non-technical learners alike. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-cloud-practitioner-training.html"><strong>WSQ - AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner Training</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book CLF-C02 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-aws-certified-cloud-practitioner-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified AI Practitioner is an foundational-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>AIF-C01</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$900 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking AIF-C01.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 100</strong> and takes 90 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>AI Practitioner is AWS''s newest foundational certification and the first vendor credential to formally certify generative AI literacy - prompt engineering, RAG, foundation model selection and responsible AI. In a market where every job description now mentions AI, it is a verifiable signal rather than a claim.</p><h2>The AIF-C01 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified AI Practitioner</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>AIF-C01</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Foundational</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>65 questions (multiple choice, multiple response and ordering)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>90 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>700 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 100 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> No prerequisites. AWS suggests up to six months of exposure to AI/ML technologies on AWS. Cloud Practitioner first is helpful but not required.</p><h2>AIF-C01 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Fundamentals of AI and ML</strong></td><td>20%</td><td>Core AI, machine learning and deep learning concepts, practical use cases, and the stages of the machine learning development lifecycle.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Fundamentals of Generative AI</strong></td><td>24%</td><td>Foundation models, tokens and embeddings, the capabilities and limitations of generative AI, and the AWS services that support generative AI workloads.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Applications of Foundation Models</strong></td><td>28%</td><td>The largest domain: selecting and evaluating foundation models, prompt engineering techniques, retrieval-augmented generation, fine-tuning approaches and Amazon Bedrock.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Guidelines for Responsible AI</strong></td><td>14%</td><td>Bias and fairness, transparency and explainability, and the tools AWS provides to identify and mitigate responsible-AI risks.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security, Compliance and Governance for AI</strong></td><td>14%</td><td>Securing AI systems and data, governance frameworks, regulatory compliance and the shared responsibility model applied to AI workloads.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-ai-practitioner-training.html">WSQ - AWS Certified AI Practitioner Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the AIF-C01 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> AI/ML Practitioner, Business Analyst, Product Manager, Solution Consultant, Developer moving into AI.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>AIF-C01</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse AIF-C01 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified AI Practitioner training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024049338</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$900</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024049338" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024049338.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024049338" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 100 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-ai-practitioner-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule AIF-C01 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The AIF-C01 exam costs USD 100 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule AIF-C01 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No prerequisites. AWS suggests up to six months of exposure to AI/ML technologies on AWS. Cloud Practitioner first is helpful but not required. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified AI Practitioner training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-ai-practitioner-training.html"><strong>WSQ - AWS Certified AI Practitioner Training</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book AIF-C01 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-aws-certified-ai-practitioner-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Associate is an associate-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>SAA-C03</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$1,500 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking SAA-C03.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 150</strong> and takes 130 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>Solutions Architect Associate is the single most in-demand AWS certification and consistently among the highest-paying IT credentials worldwide. It is the credential that moves you from ''can use AWS'' to ''can design on AWS'', and it is the one most Singapore cloud job postings name explicitly.</p><h2>The SAA-C03 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>SAA-C03</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>65 questions (multiple choice and multiple response)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>130 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>720 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 150 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> AWS recommends at least one year of hands-on experience designing on AWS. Cloud Practitioner is a useful precursor but is not required.</p><h2>SAA-C03 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Design Secure Architectures</strong></td><td>30%</td><td>The largest domain: secure access to AWS resources with IAM, secure workloads and application tiers, and appropriate data security controls including encryption at rest and in transit.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Design Resilient Architectures</strong></td><td>26%</td><td>Scalable and loosely coupled architectures, highly available and fault-tolerant designs, decoupling with SQS/SNS/EventBridge, and multi-AZ and multi-Region strategies.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Design High-Performing Architectures</strong></td><td>24%</td><td>Choosing performant storage, compute, database and networking solutions, and designing data ingestion and transformation for the workload at hand.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Design Cost-Optimized Architectures</strong></td><td>20%</td><td>Cost-effective storage, compute, database and network architectures, right-sizing, and selecting the correct pricing model for the workload.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the CASL course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/casl-aws-certified-solutions-architect-associate-training.html">CASL - AWS Certified Solutions Architect Associate Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the SAA-C03 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a CASL-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Solutions Architect, Cloud Engineer, DevOps Engineer, Technical Lead, Systems Engineer.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>SAA-C03</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse SAA-C03 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Associate training</h2><p>This is a <strong>CASL-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2026064535</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$1,500</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline CASL course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2026064535" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>3. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>4. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>5. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 150 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/casl-aws-certified-solutions-architect-associate-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule SAA-C03 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the CASL assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the CASL assessment. The SAA-C03 exam costs USD 150 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>CASL assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. PSEA and UTAP can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule SAA-C03 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>AWS recommends at least one year of hands-on experience designing on AWS. Cloud Practitioner is a useful precursor but is not required. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Associate training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/casl-aws-certified-solutions-architect-associate-training.html"><strong>CASL - AWS Certified Solutions Architect Associate Training</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book SAA-C03 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'casl-aws-certified-solutions-architect-associate-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified Data Engineer - Associate is an associate-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>DEA-C01</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$1,500 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking DEA-C01.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 150</strong> and takes 130 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>Data Engineer Associate replaced the retired Data Analytics Specialty and is now AWS''s dedicated data credential. Data engineering is one of the hardest roles in Singapore to hire for, and this certification validates the pipeline, storage and governance skills that employers cannot easily assess in an interview.</p><h2>The DEA-C01 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified Data Engineer - Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>DEA-C01</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>65 questions (multiple choice and multiple response)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>130 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>720 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 150 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> AWS recommends two to three years of data engineering experience and one to two years of hands-on AWS experience.</p><h2>DEA-C01 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Data Ingestion and Transformation</strong></td><td>34%</td><td>The largest domain: ingesting streaming and batch data, transforming and processing it with Glue, EMR and Lambda, orchestrating pipelines, and programming concepts including SQL and infrastructure as code.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Data Store Management</strong></td><td>26%</td><td>Choosing the right data store, understanding data cataloguing systems, managing the data lifecycle, and designing schemas and schema evolution.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Data Operations and Support</strong></td><td>22%</td><td>Automating data processing with AWS services, analysing data with Athena and Redshift, maintaining and monitoring pipelines, and ensuring data quality.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Data Security and Governance</strong></td><td>18%</td><td>Authentication and authorisation, data encryption and masking, audit logging, and meeting privacy and governance requirements.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-data-engineer-associate-training.html">WSQ - AWS Certified Data Engineer Associate Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the DEA-C01 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Data Engineer, Analytics Engineer, ETL Developer, Data Platform Engineer, Database Administrator.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>DEA-C01</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse DEA-C01 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified Data Engineer - Associate training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2025053209</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$1,500</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2025053209" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2025053209.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2025053209" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 150 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-data-engineer-associate-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule DEA-C01 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The DEA-C01 exam costs USD 150 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule DEA-C01 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>AWS recommends two to three years of data engineering experience and one to two years of hands-on AWS experience. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified Data Engineer - Associate training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-data-engineer-associate-training.html"><strong>WSQ - AWS Certified Data Engineer Associate Training</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book DEA-C01 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-aws-certified-data-engineer-associate-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified Developer - Associate is an associate-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>DVA-C02</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$1,500 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking DVA-C02.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 150</strong> and takes 130 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>Developer Associate is the credential that proves you can build on AWS rather than just deploy to it - Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB, CI/CD and observability. For software engineers, it is the most directly job-relevant AWS certification and the natural companion to Solutions Architect Associate.</p><h2>The DVA-C02 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified Developer - Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>DVA-C02</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>65 questions (multiple choice and multiple response)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>130 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>720 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 150 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> AWS recommends at least one year of hands-on experience developing and maintaining AWS applications, plus proficiency in at least one high-level programming language.</p><h2>DVA-C02 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Development with AWS Services</strong></td><td>32%</td><td>The largest domain: writing code for serverless applications with Lambda, working with data stores, and developing event-driven and API-driven solutions.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security</strong></td><td>26%</td><td>Implementing authentication and authorisation with Cognito and IAM, encrypting data in transit and at rest, and managing secrets with Secrets Manager and Parameter Store.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Deployment</strong></td><td>24%</td><td>Preparing application artefacts, testing in development environments, automating deployment with CodePipeline and CodeDeploy, and using infrastructure as code such as SAM and CloudFormation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Troubleshooting and Optimization</strong></td><td>18%</td><td>Root cause analysis with CloudWatch and X-Ray, code instrumentation for observability, and optimising application performance on AWS.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-developer-associate-training.html">WSQ - AWS Certified Developer Associate Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the DVA-C02 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Cloud Developer, Backend Engineer, Serverless Developer, DevOps Engineer, Software Engineer.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>DVA-C02</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse DVA-C02 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified Developer - Associate training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2025052675</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$1,500</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2025052675" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2025052675.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2025052675" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 150 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-developer-associate-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule DVA-C02 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The DVA-C02 exam costs USD 150 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule DVA-C02 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>AWS recommends at least one year of hands-on experience developing and maintaining AWS applications, plus proficiency in at least one high-level programming language. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified Developer - Associate training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-developer-associate-training.html"><strong>WSQ - AWS Certified Developer Associate Training</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book DVA-C02 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-aws-certified-developer-associate-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified SysOps Administrator - Associate is an associate-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>SOA-C02</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$1,500 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking SOA-C02.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 150</strong> and takes 130 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>SysOps Administrator is the operations-focused associate certification - it certifies that you can run, monitor and troubleshoot AWS workloads in production, not just design them. It is the natural credential for infrastructure and support engineers moving into cloud.</p><h2>The SOA-C02 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified SysOps Administrator - Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>SOA-C02</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>65 questions (multiple choice and multiple response)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>130 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>720 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 150 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> AWS recommends at least one year of hands-on experience operating and managing workloads on AWS.</p><h2>SOA-C02 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Monitoring, Logging and Remediation</strong></td><td>20%</td><td>Implementing metrics, alarms and filters with CloudWatch, and remediating problems based on monitoring and availability metrics.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reliability and Business Continuity</strong></td><td>16%</td><td>Implementing scalability and elasticity, high availability and fault tolerance, and backup and restore strategies.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Deployment, Provisioning and Automation</strong></td><td>18%</td><td>Provisioning cloud resources, automating manual or repeatable processes, and managing infrastructure with CloudFormation and Systems Manager.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security and Compliance</strong></td><td>16%</td><td>Implementing and managing security and compliance policies, data and infrastructure protection strategies, and IAM at operational scale.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Networking and Content Delivery</strong></td><td>18%</td><td>Implementing networking features and connectivity, configuring domains, DNS services and content delivery, and troubleshooting network connectivity.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cost and Performance Optimization</strong></td><td>12%</td><td>Implementing cost optimisation strategies and performance optimisation strategies across the running estate.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-sysops-administrator-associate-training.html">WSQ - AWS Certified SysOps Administrator Associate Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the SOA-C02 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Cloud Operations Engineer, Systems Administrator, Site Reliability Engineer, Infrastructure Engineer, NOC Engineer.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>SOA-C02</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse SOA-C02 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified SysOps Administrator - Associate training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024051413</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$1,500</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024051413" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024051413.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024051413" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 150 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-sysops-administrator-associate-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule SOA-C02 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The SOA-C02 exam costs USD 150 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule SOA-C02 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>AWS recommends at least one year of hands-on experience operating and managing workloads on AWS. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified SysOps Administrator - Associate training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-sysops-administrator-associate-training.html"><strong>WSQ - AWS Certified SysOps Administrator Associate Training</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book SOA-C02 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-aws-certified-sysops-administrator-associate-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer - Associate is an associate-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>MLA-C01</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$1,500 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking MLA-C01.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 150</strong> and takes 130 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>ML Engineer Associate is AWS''s answer to the gap between data science and production - it certifies MLOps: deploying, orchestrating, monitoring and securing models, not just training them. That operational half is exactly where most ML projects fail and where hiring demand is concentrated.</p><h2>The MLA-C01 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer - Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>MLA-C01</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Associate</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>65 questions (multiple choice, multiple response, ordering and matching)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>130 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>720 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 150 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> AWS recommends at least one year of experience using Amazon SageMaker and other ML engineering AWS services.</p><h2>MLA-C01 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Data Preparation for Machine Learning</strong></td><td>28%</td><td>Ingesting and storing data, transforming data and performing feature engineering, and ensuring data integrity and preparing data for modelling including bias detection.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>ML Model Development</strong></td><td>26%</td><td>Choosing a modelling approach, training and refining models, and analysing model performance with the appropriate evaluation metrics.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Deployment and Orchestration of ML Workflows</strong></td><td>22%</td><td>Selecting a deployment infrastructure, creating and scripting infrastructure, and building automated CI/CD pipelines for machine learning.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>ML Solution Monitoring, Maintenance and Security</strong></td><td>24%</td><td>Monitoring models and infrastructure for drift and cost, securing AWS ML resources, and maintaining models in production.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-machine-learning-engineer-associate-training.html">WSQ - AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer Associate Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the MLA-C01 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Machine Learning Engineer, MLOps Engineer, Data Scientist, AI Engineer, Data Engineer moving into ML.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>MLA-C01</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse MLA-C01 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer - Associate training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2024049340</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$1,500</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2024049340" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2024049340.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2024049340" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 150 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-machine-learning-engineer-associate-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule MLA-C01 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The MLA-C01 exam costs USD 150 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule MLA-C01 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>AWS recommends at least one year of experience using Amazon SageMaker and other ML engineering AWS services. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer - Associate training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-machine-learning-engineer-associate-training.html"><strong>WSQ - AWS Certified Machine Learning Engineer Associate Training</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book MLA-C01 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-aws-certified-machine-learning-engineer-associate-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified DevOps Engineer - Professional is an professional-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>DOP-C02</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,000 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking DOP-C02.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 300</strong> and takes 180 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>DevOps Engineer Professional is one of AWS''s two professional-level certifications and among the most respected credentials in cloud. It certifies that you can automate an entire delivery pipeline - build, deploy, monitor, recover - which is why it commands one of the highest salary premiums of any IT certification.</p><h2>The DOP-C02 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified DevOps Engineer - Professional</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>DOP-C02</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Professional</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>75 questions (multiple choice and multiple response)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>180 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>750 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 300 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> AWS recommends two or more years of experience provisioning, operating and managing AWS environments, plus proficiency in at least one high-level programming language.</p><h2>DOP-C02 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>SDLC Automation</strong></td><td>22%</td><td>CI/CD pipelines with CodePipeline and CodeBuild, automated testing strategies, artefact management, and deployment strategies including blue/green and canary.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Configuration Management and IaC</strong></td><td>17%</td><td>Defining and deploying infrastructure as code with CloudFormation and CDK, managing multi-account environments, and reusable, scalable configuration.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Resilient Cloud Solutions</strong></td><td>15%</td><td>Implementing highly available solutions, automating scaling, and designing and automating disaster recovery strategies.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Monitoring and Logging</strong></td><td>15%</td><td>Configuring logging and metrics collection, auditing and analysing logs and metrics, and automating monitoring and event management.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Incident and Event Response</strong></td><td>14%</td><td>Managing event sources, implementing automated healing, and setting up the automated response to operational incidents.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security and Compliance</strong></td><td>17%</td><td>Implementing identity and access management at scale, automating security controls and governance, and automating compliance and audit reporting.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-devops-engineering-on-aws.html">WSQ - DevOps Engineering on AWS</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the DOP-C02 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> DevOps Engineer, Site Reliability Engineer, Platform Engineer, Cloud Automation Engineer, Release Engineer.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our test centre</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>DOP-C02</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified DevOps Engineer - Professional training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2023040474</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2023040474" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2023040474.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2023040474" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 300 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-devops-engineering-on-aws.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule DOP-C02 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The DOP-C02 exam costs USD 300 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit and PSEA can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule DOP-C02 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>AWS recommends two or more years of experience provisioning, operating and managing AWS environments, plus proficiency in at least one high-level programming language. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified DevOps Engineer - Professional training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-devops-engineering-on-aws.html"><strong>WSQ - DevOps Engineering on AWS</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book DOP-C02 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-devops-engineering-on-aws-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Professional is an professional-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>SAP-C02</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,000 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking SAP-C02.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 300</strong> and takes 180 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>Solutions Architect Professional is the most senior architecture credential AWS offers and routinely tops industry salary surveys. It certifies design judgement across multi-account, hybrid and migration scenarios - the problems that define enterprise cloud work rather than single-workload design.</p><h2>The SAP-C02 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Professional</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>SAP-C02</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Professional</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>75 questions (multiple choice and multiple response)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>180 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>750 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 300 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> AWS recommends two or more years of hands-on experience designing and managing AWS solutions. Solutions Architect Associate first is strongly advised.</p><h2>SAP-C02 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Design Solutions for Organizational Complexity</strong></td><td>26%</td><td>Network connectivity across complex estates, multi-account AWS environments with Organizations and Control Tower, and centralised security and governance.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Design for New Solutions</strong></td><td>29%</td><td>The largest domain: designing deployment strategies, business continuity, security controls, reliability and performance for greenfield workloads that meet stated business requirements.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Continuous Improvement for Existing Solutions</strong></td><td>25%</td><td>Improving operational excellence, security, performance, reliability and cost efficiency of workloads already running in production.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Accelerate Workload Migration and Modernization</strong></td><td>20%</td><td>Selecting migration strategies, determining the optimal migration approach for existing workloads, and modernising legacy applications to cloud-native patterns.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-solutions-architect-professional-training.html">WSQ - AWS Certified Solutions Architect Professional Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the SAP-C02 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> Principal Solutions Architect, Cloud Architect, Enterprise Architect, Technical Lead, Cloud Consultant.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>SAP-C02</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse SAP-C02 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Professional training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2025053926</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2025053926" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2025053926.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2025053926" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 300 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-solutions-architect-professional-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule SAP-C02 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The SAP-C02 exam costs USD 300 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule SAP-C02 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>AWS recommends two or more years of hands-on experience designing and managing AWS solutions. Solutions Architect Associate first is strongly advised. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Professional training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-solutions-architect-professional-training.html"><strong>WSQ - AWS Certified Solutions Architect Professional Training</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book SAP-C02 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-aws-certified-solutions-architect-professional-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';

UPDATE mmd_blog_post SET content = '<div class="mmd-summary"><div class="mmd-summary-label">Summary</div><p>AWS Certified DevOps Engineer - Professional is an professional-level AWS credential and one of the most recognised certifications in cloud computing. This guide makes the case for actually sitting <strong>DOP-C02</strong>, breaks down every exam domain and its weighting, and sets out the funding that brings the S$2,000 course fee down sharply for eligible learners. AWS exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a <strong>Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong> - so you can train and sit the exam at the same address.</p></div><h2>Why you should actually sit the exam</h2><p>Plenty of people attend cloud training and never book the exam. That is the single biggest waste in professional development, because <strong>the training teaches you the skill, but only the certification is visible to anyone else</strong>. Here is the honest case for booking DOP-C02.</p><ul><li><strong>Recruiters filter on it before a human reads your CV.</strong> Search any Singapore job board for cloud roles and the certification is named in the requirements. Applicant tracking systems match on that string. Without the credential you are often filtered out before your experience is ever assessed.</li><li><strong>It is externally verifiable.</strong> Anyone can claim AWS experience. An AWS certification is issued by Amazon, carries a verification number, and can be checked by an employer in seconds. That asymmetry is precisely why it carries weight.</li><li><strong>It pays.</strong> AWS certifications appear year after year at the top of global IT salary surveys, with the professional-level credentials among the highest paying of any certification in technology. The exam fee is a rounding error against a single salary revision.</li><li><strong>The deadline is what makes you learn.</strong> A booked exam date converts good intentions into study. Learners who book the exam before the course ends pass at far higher rates than those who leave it open-ended, because the material is still fresh and there is a date to work towards.</li><li><strong>It benefits your employer directly.</strong> AWS Partner Network membership tiers are calculated from the number of certified staff an organisation holds. Your certification is a business asset, which is a persuasive argument when asking your company to sponsor the exam fee.</li><li><strong>It compounds.</strong> AWS certifications ladder deliberately - foundational to associate to professional and specialty. Each one you hold makes the next materially easier, and the ladder is the clearest structured path in cloud.</li></ul><p>The exam costs <strong>USD 300</strong> and takes 180 minutes. Set against the salary and mobility it unlocks - and against a course fee that funding already reduces sharply - it is one of the highest-return decisions available to a technology professional in Singapore. <strong>Book it before you finish the course.</strong></p><p>One practical note: AWS gives every certification holder a <strong>50% discount voucher towards their next exam</strong>, plus access to official practice material. Passing one exam makes the next one cheaper, so the ladder gets less expensive as you climb it.</p><h2>Why AWS certifications carry weight</h2><p>AWS has held the largest share of the global cloud infrastructure market for over a decade, and Singapore is one of its most established regions - AWS has operated an Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region since 2010 and has committed billions to local infrastructure. The practical consequence for your career is simple: <strong>more Singapore employers run workloads on AWS than on any other cloud</strong>, so an AWS credential is the one most likely to match the stack you will actually be hired to work on.</p><ul><li><strong>Role-based, not product-trivia.</strong> AWS certifications are built from job-task analysis of real roles, so the exam tests the decisions the role requires rather than memorised service limits.</li><li><strong>Scenario-based questions.</strong> Associate and professional exams present multi-sentence scenarios with several technically valid answers, and ask for the best one given cost, resilience or security constraints. That is hard to pass without real understanding.</li><li><strong>A deliberate ladder.</strong> Foundational, associate, professional and specialty tiers give a structured progression, each level building on the last.</li><li><strong>Recertification keeps it current.</strong> Credentials are valid for three years, so a current certification means current knowledge - which is exactly why employers trust it in a field that changes this quickly.</li></ul><p>DevOps Engineer Professional certifies end-to-end delivery automation on AWS at professional level - the pipelines, infrastructure as code, monitoring and automated recovery that keep production systems shipping safely. It is one of the highest-paying certifications in the industry and a clear differentiator for senior engineering roles.</p><h2>The DOP-C02 exam at a glance</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Certification</th><td>AWS Certified DevOps Engineer - Professional</td></tr><tr><th>Exam code</th><td>DOP-C02</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Professional</td></tr><tr><th>Format</th><td>75 questions (multiple choice and multiple response)</td></tr><tr><th>Duration</th><td>180 minutes</td></tr><tr><th>Passing score</th><td>750 out of 1000</td></tr><tr><th>Exam fee</th><td>USD 300 (paid to AWS, not included in the course fee)</td></tr><tr><th>Validity</th><td>Valid for 3 years</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Recommended background.</strong> AWS recommends two or more years of experience provisioning, operating and managing AWS environments, plus proficiency in at least one high-level programming language.</p><h2>DOP-C02 exam domains and weightings</h2><p>Read the weightings as a study budget. The heaviest domain deserves proportionally more of your practice time, and on a scored exam it is where marks are won or lost.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Exam domain</th><th>Weighting</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>SDLC Automation</strong></td><td>22%</td><td>CI/CD pipelines with CodePipeline and CodeBuild, automated testing strategies, artefact management, and deployment strategies including blue/green and canary.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Configuration Management and IaC</strong></td><td>17%</td><td>Defining and deploying infrastructure as code with CloudFormation and CDK, managing multi-account environments, and reusable, scalable configuration.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Resilient Cloud Solutions</strong></td><td>15%</td><td>Implementing highly available solutions, automating scaling, and designing and automating disaster recovery strategies.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Monitoring and Logging</strong></td><td>15%</td><td>Configuring logging and metrics collection, auditing and analysing logs and metrics, and automating monitoring and event management.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Incident and Event Response</strong></td><td>14%</td><td>Managing event sources, implementing automated healing, and setting up the automated response to operational incidents.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Security and Compliance</strong></td><td>17%</td><td>Implementing identity and access management at scale, automating security controls and governance, and automating compliance and audit reporting.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What the WSQ course covers</h2><p>Our <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-devops-engineer-training.html">WSQ - AWS Certified DevOps Engineer Professional Training</a> is instructor-led and hands-on, mapped to the DOP-C02 objectives above and delivered in our Woodlands Square training centre, with live online and hybrid options available. Because it is a WSQ-approved programme it carries the funding below and is assessed, so you leave with a Statement of Attainment as well as exam readiness.</p><p><strong>Typical roles this leads to:</strong> DevOps Engineer, Site Reliability Engineer, Platform Engineer, Cloud Automation Engineer, Release Engineer.</p><h2>Sit your exam at our centre &mdash; and practise free before you do</h2><p>You do not need to go anywhere else to sit the exam. <strong>Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center</strong>, and AWS certification exams are delivered through the Pearson VUE network &mdash; so you can book and sit your proctored <strong>DOP-C02</strong> exam at our training centre at 12 Woodlands Square, in the same room you studied in.</p><p><strong>Bonus: register for this course and you get free practice exams.</strong> Course participants get access to our <a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practice Exam Portal</a>, where you can rehearse DOP-C02 questions in realistic <strong>Practice Mode</strong> and under timed <strong>Exam Mode</strong> conditions, then <strong>retake them as many times as you like</strong> before the real thing.</p><p>This matters more than it sounds. The single best predictor of passing a certification exam first time is how many realistic practice questions you sat beforehand &mdash; not how many hours of content you watched. Practising under timed conditions is also what stops the clock from being the thing that beats you on exam day.</p><p><a href="https://exams.tertiaryinfotech.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Start practising at exams.tertiaryinfotech.com &rarr;</strong></a></p><h2>What you will actually pay: funding for AWS Certified DevOps Engineer - Professional training</h2><p>This is a <strong>WSQ-approved course (course reference <code>TGS-2025054815</code>)</strong>, so the published fee of <strong>S$2,000</strong> is not what most learners pay. The schemes stack, applied in order: baseline subsidy first, then credits and claims against the balance.</p><h3>1. Baseline WSQ course fee funding</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents receive <strong>up to 70% course fee funding</strong>. Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above qualify for <strong>up to 90% under the Mid-Career Enhanced Subsidy (MCES)</strong>. SME-sponsored employees may also qualify for the enhanced rate. Funding is subject to eligibility and to meeting the attendance and assessment requirements.</p><h3>2. SkillsFuture Credit (SFC)</h3><p>Singapore Citizens aged 25 and above can offset the <em>remaining</em> fee payable after funding with their SkillsFuture Credit. Note the restriction: the $4,000 Additional SkillsFuture Credit (Mid-Career Support) cannot be used on this course. You can <a href="https://courses.myskillsfuture.gov.sg/courses/TGS-2025054815" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apply directly on the MySkillsFuture portal</a> using course code TGS-2025054815.</p><h3>3. SkillsFuture Enterprise Credit (SFEC)</h3><p>Sponsoring employees? Eligible Singapore-registered companies can draw on <strong>up to $10,000 of SFEC</strong> to cover out-of-pocket costs. Look the course up on <a href="https://skillsfuture.gobusiness.gov.sg/course-directory/courses/TGS-2025054815" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SkillsFuture for Business</a>.</p><h3>4. PSEA</h3><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens can pay the remaining fee from their <strong>Post-Secondary Education Account</strong>. Check the course listing on MySkillsFuture and look under &ldquo;Keyword Tags&rdquo; for a PSEA tag to confirm eligibility, then submit a PSEA withdrawal form to us.</p><h3>5. UTAP</h3><p>NTUC members can claim <strong>50% of the unfunded course fee</strong> through the Union Training Assistance Programme, capped at $250 per year, or <strong>$500 per year for members aged 40 and above</strong>. Claims are submitted after course completion via the <a href="https://utap.ntuc.org.sg/onlineClaim" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NTUC UTAP portal</a>. UTAP support is subject to the course remaining UTAP-eligible at the time of your claim.</p><h3>6. Absentee Payroll</h3><p>Employers sponsoring staff may claim <strong>Absentee Payroll</strong> to offset the salary cost of the hours their employee spends in training, subject to the prevailing SSG rates and caps.</p><p><em>The AWS exam fee of USD 300 is paid separately to AWS and is not covered by course fee funding. All funding is subject to eligibility and to prevailing SSG policies at the time of course commencement - talk to us and we will work out your exact nett fee.</em></p><h2>Your route to certification</h2><ol><li><strong>Check your funding eligibility.</strong> Citizenship, age band and employer sponsorship determine whether you pay 30%, 10% or less of the published fee.</li><li><strong>Register for the course.</strong> Pick a class date on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-devops-engineer-training.html">course page</a> and reserve your seat.</li><li><strong>Book the exam before the course ends.</strong> Create an AWS Certification account, schedule DOP-C02 through Pearson VUE, and pick our test centre. A booked date is what turns intent into a pass.</li><li><strong>Attend the training.</strong> Complete the hands-on labs and the WSQ assessment to earn your Statement of Attainment.</li><li><strong>Sit the exam while it is fresh.</strong> Ideally within two to four weeks of the course, at our Pearson VUE centre.</li><li><strong>Claim what you are entitled to.</strong> Offset with SkillsFuture Credit or PSEA, and submit your UTAP claim after completion. Then use your 50% AWS retake-or-next-exam voucher to climb the ladder.</li></ol><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Is the AWS exam fee included in the course fee?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. The course fee covers instructor-led training, courseware and the WSQ assessment. The DOP-C02 exam costs USD 300 and is paid directly to AWS when you schedule through Pearson VUE. You can sit it at our own Pearson VUE test centre.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I have to pass the AWS exam to get the funding?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. Course fee funding depends on attending the course and being assessed competent in the <em>WSQ assessment</em>, not on the AWS exam result. Meeting the minimum attendance requirement and passing the assessment secures your subsidy and your Statement of Attainment.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What will I actually pay for the course?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Eligible Singapore Citizens and PRs receive up to 70% funding, rising to up to 90% for Singapore Citizens aged 40 and above under MCES. SkillsFuture Credit, PSEA and UTAP can be applied to the balance. Send us your details and we will confirm your exact nett fee before you commit.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I sit the AWS exam at your centre?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. AWS certification exams are delivered through Pearson VUE, and Tertiary Infotech Academy is a Pearson VUE Authorized Test Center. Schedule DOP-C02 through your AWS Certification account and select our centre at 12 Woodlands Square. Online proctored delivery via OnVUE is also available if you prefer to sit it remotely.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need the recommended experience before enrolling?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>AWS recommends two or more years of experience provisioning, operating and managing AWS environments, plus proficiency in at least one high-level programming language. AWS recommendations are guidance, not gates - nothing prevents you from enrolling or from sitting the exam. If you are unsure whether to start here or a tier lower, talk to us and we will point you at the right course.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What happens if I fail the exam?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>You may retake it after a 14-day waiting period, and there is no limit on attempts, though each retake is charged at full price. This is the practical argument for sitting the exam soon after training rather than months later - your first attempt is much more likely to be your only one.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">How long is the certification valid?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Valid for 3 years. AWS will prompt you to recertify before expiry, and holding a current certification is what signals current knowledge to an employer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Register for AWS Certified DevOps Engineer - Professional training</h2><p>Classes fill ahead of each intake. View upcoming dates and reserve your place on the <a href="https://www.tertiarycourses.com.sg/wsq-aws-certified-devops-engineer-training.html"><strong>WSQ - AWS Certified DevOps Engineer Professional Training</strong></a> course page, or call +65 6100 0613 and we will work out your funding first. Then book DOP-C02 - the training is only worth what the certificate proves.</p>'
WHERE url_key = 'wsq-aws-certified-devops-engineer-professional-training-singapore-guide' AND content NOT LIKE '%exams.tertiaryinfotech.com%';
